# Control specs (SPEC-00–10)

Full text: `docs/spec-references/SPEC-00-INDEX-and-conventions.md` and `SPEC-01` through `SPEC-10` in that folder. Call them by those filenames.

These are per-control contracts (340 controls). The execution queue for them is `docs/spec-references/BP-00-INDEX-and-rules.md` (BP-01 through BP-13, one prompt per session). A SPEC is the contract. A BP is the only permission to change code, and only after the user feeds that BP. `spec-reconciliation-overlay.md` still wins on conflict. BP-01 through BP-13 are not in the repo until each one is fed.

## Conventions (every chunk inherits these)

1. Paid calls (FAL, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, Tripo, Runway, Suno) go through `providerSubmit` / `submitToFal` / `claudeCall`, pause-aware, source-attributed.
2. Timeline clips write the one store. Do not add another.
3. Model payload params come from the live schema via `buildPayload`. Do not hardcode ranges.
4. Honest UI. If the backend is coarse, the control is coarse.
5. Camera, style, and character intent are stored as structured data and rendered to a prompt.
6. The spine is shared. Heavy controls are desktop-only. Note the other host.

